{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetRMkQeNGpNkuSFW7w9J","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my analysis, I now have a clear understanding of the system. Let me move to the design phase.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt**: Add `OrderStatus` enum with `ACTIVE` and `CANCELLED` values, and add `status: OrderStatus = OrderStatus.ACTIVE` field to the `Order` data class.\n\n2. **OrderRepository.kt**: Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` - actually no, that's backwards. I need to find shipments by order ID from the shipment repository. Let me revise - I don't need to change OrderRepository, just add a method to ShipmentRepository.\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt**: Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to find all shipments for an order.\n\n4. **ApiError.kt**: Add two new ErrorCode values:\n   - `ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED` - when trying to cancel an order with CONFIRMED shipments\n   - `ORDER_IS_CANCELLED` - when trying to create a shipment for a cancelled order\n\n5. **OrderController.kt**: Add `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` endpoint that:\n   - Finds the order, throwing ResourceNotFoundException if not found\n   - If already CANCELLED, return the order (idempotent)\n   - Check all shipments for the order: if any is CONFIRMED, throw ConflictException and change nothing\n   - Otherwise, set order status to CANCELLED, update all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED, save all changes, return the cancelled order\n\n6. **ShipmentController.kt**: In the `create()` method, before saving the shipment, check if the order exists and is CANCELLED. If so, throw ConflictException with ORDER_IS_CANCELLED.\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Add tests for:\n   - Cancelling an ACTIVE order returns the order with CANCELLED status\n   - Cancelling a CANCELLED order again succeeds (idempotent)\n   - Attempting to cancel when a shipment is CONFIRMED returns 409 with error envelope\n   - Cancelling a non-existent order returns 404\n   - Getting a cancelled order returns status CANCELLED\n\n8. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add test for:\n   - Attempting to create a shipment for a cancelled order returns 409 with appropriate error code\n\n**Alternative approach rejected:**\n\nI considered making the cancel operation a service layer method, but this repository is already minimal and all logic stays in controllers. I'll keep the cancel logic in the OrderController for consistency with the existing create/read patterns.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n1. **Successful cancel of ACTIVE order:**\n   - POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n   - Controller finds order (404 if not found)\n   - Get all shipments for orderId\n   - Check if any shipment is CONFIRMED → if yes, throw ConflictException(409), no changes\n   - If no CONFIRMED shipments: set order.status = CANCELLED, update all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED\n   - Save updated order to repository\n   - Return ResponseEntity.ok(updatedOrder)\n\n2. **Idempotent cancel (already CANCELLED):**\n   - POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n   - Find order\n   - If status is CANCELLED, immediately return it (no shipment changes)\n   - Return ResponseEntity.ok(order)\n\n3. **Cancel with CONFIRMED shipment:**\n   - Find order\n   - Get shipments, detect CONFIRMED\n   - Throw ConflictException(ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED, message)\n   - Return 409 with error envelope\n   - No database changes\n\n4. **Create shipment on cancelled order:**\n   - POST /shipments with orderId that points to CANCELLED order\n   - ShipmentController.create checks if order exists and is CANCELLED\n   - Throw ConflictException(ORDER_IS_CANCELLED, message)\n   - Return 409 with error envelope\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. `cancelsAnActiveOrder()` - Create order, cancel it, verify status is CANCELLED and shipments CREATED→CANCELLED\n2. `cancelIsIdempotent()` - Cancel twice, second succeeds with no changes\n3. `rejectsLiftoffWithConfirmedShipment()` - Create shipment, confirm it, cancel order → 409, order still ACTIVE\n4. `rejectsUnknownOrder()` - Cancel non-existent order → 404\n5. `returnsConfirmedCancelledOrder()` - Cancel order, GET it back, verify CANCELLED status\n6. `rejectsShipmentCreationForCancelledOrder()` - Create and cancel order, attempt to create shipment → 409\n\nNow I'll proceed to implementation.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nLet me start by adding the OrderStatus enum and updating the Order class:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2679,"cache_read_input_tokens":21510,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2679},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f3d372dc-63f6-4723-9c06-276e957184e7","uuid":"f1cc6df1-53a1-4f17-9581-549a396bd6d2","timestamp":"2026-09-09T19:30:58.712Z","request_id":"req_011CetRMjkwf5md54NVGJkUw"}
