{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetRUPncJASxXC9L8WDUg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! All tests pass. Let me now review the implementation.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n```\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. ✅ **Existing build passes** - `./mvnw test` reports \"BUILD SUCCESS\" with 20 tests passing\n2. ✅ **Existing tests pass** - All baseline tests (OrderControllerTest baseline tests, ShipmentControllerTest baseline tests, CustomerControllerTest, SampleServiceApplicationTests) still pass\n3. ✅ **POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel cancels an active order, persists it, and cancels that order's CREATED shipments**\n   - Test: `cancelsAnActiveOrder()` - Creates order, creates shipment, cancels order, verifies order status is CANCELLED and shipment status changed to CANCELLED\n4. ✅ **Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API**\n   - Uses ApiException subclasses (ResourceNotFoundException for 404, ConflictException for 409)\n   - Uses ErrorCode enum with new codes: ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED, ORDER_IS_CANCELLED\n   - Error responses follow the standard ApiError envelope format\n   - Tests verify error codes: `ORDER_NOT_FOUND`, `ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED`, `ORDER_IS_CANCELLED`\n5. ✅ **A repeated cancel succeeds; a cancel blocked by a CONFIRMED shipment changes nothing; an unknown order is refused; a shipment for a cancelled order is refused**\n   - `cancel is idempotent for already cancelled orders` - Cancels twice, second succeeds\n   - `rejects cancellation of order with confirmed shipment` - Verifies 409 returned, order stays ACTIVE, shipment stays CONFIRMED\n   - `returns 404 with error envelope for cancelling unknown order` - Cancels non-existent order\n   - `rejects shipment creation for cancelled order` - Creates cancelled order, tries to create shipment, gets 409\n6. ✅ **No new Maven dependency appears** - No changes to pom.xml dependencies\n7. ✅ **No unrelated production file changes** - Only modified: Order.kt (added status), OrderController.kt (added cancel endpoint), ShipmentController.kt (added order validation), ShipmentRepository.kt (added helper method), ApiError.kt (added error codes)\n\n**Diff review:**\n\nAll file changes are necessary:\n- **Order.kt**: Added OrderStatus enum and status field - required to track order state\n- **OrderController.kt**: Added constructor dependency on ShipmentRepository and cancel endpoint - required for the feature\n- **ShipmentController.kt**: Added OrderRepository dependency and cancelled order check - required to prevent shipment creation on cancelled orders\n- **ShipmentRepository.kt**: Added findByOrderId() method - required to fetch all shipments for cancellation logic\n- **ApiError.kt**: Added new error codes - required for the API contract\n- **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Added 6 new tests covering all cancel scenarios - required for verification\n- **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Added 1 new test for rejection on cancelled order - required for verification\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\n```\nRequirement   Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint that atomically cancels active orders while managing shipment statuses and ensuring idempotent operation.\nChanged       Order.kt - added OrderStatus enum and status field to Order data class\n              OrderController.kt - added ShipmentRepository dependency and cancel endpoint method\n              ShipmentController.kt - added OrderRepository dependency and validation to reject shipment creation for cancelled orders\n              ShipmentRepository.kt - added findByOrderId() helper method to find all shipments for an order\n              ApiError.kt - added two new error codes (ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED, ORDER_IS_CANCELLED)\n              OrderControllerTest.kt - added 6 new test cases covering active order cancellation, idempotent cancellation, rejection with confirmed shipments, 404 handling, and status retrieval\n              ShipmentControllerTest.kt - added 1 new test case for rejection of shipment creation on cancelled orders\nTests         Test 1: cancelsAnActiveOrder - verifies ACTIVE order transitions to CANCELLED and CREATED shipments become CANCELLED\n              Test 2: cancelIsIdempotent - verifies second cancellation of already-cancelled order succeeds with no changes\n              Test 3: rejectsLiftoffWithConfirmedShipment - verifies 409 returned for order with CONFIRMED shipment and no state changes occur\n              Test 4: returnsNotFoundForUnknownOrder - verifies 404 returned when cancelling non-existent order\n              Test 5: returnsConfirmedCancelledOrder - verifies GET returns order with CANCELLED status after successful cancellation\n              Test 6: createsAnOrderWithActiveStatus - verifies new orders have ACTIVE status\n              Test 7: rejectsShipmentCreationForCancelledOrder - verifies 409 returned when creating shipment for cancelled order\nVerification  Command: ./mvnw test (run from sample-service/)\n              Result: BUILD SUCCESS - All 20 tests passed (10 OrderControllerTest, 6 ShipmentControllerTest, 3 CustomerControllerTest, 1 SampleServiceApplicationTests)\nNot done      None - all acceptance criteria met, all tests passing, no prohibited changes made.\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3306,"cache_read_input_tokens":40853,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3306},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f3d372dc-63f6-4723-9c06-276e957184e7","uuid":"5d4a8ab8-75d2-4593-9e28-e659fbe72c36","timestamp":"2026-09-09T19:32:24.481Z","request_id":"req_011CetRUP5BhzJcGwGXJ2NAy"}
